  "slug": "states-chiral-hoti-98d5",
  "summary": "Recent preprints connect accidental bound states in the continuum to radiation-source parity and spatial nonlocality in open photonic systems.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the characterization of bound states in the continuum (BICs), localized modes that persist within the radiation continuum of open photonic systems. Two items address accidental BICs directly: one shows that in vertically asymmetric photonic lattices they are governed by radiation-source parity and recovered through radiation-source parity restoration, while the other models metasurface BICs as converging reflection and transmission zeros and argues that accidental BICs require spatially nonlocal response. A third study examines Berry phase and topological quasi-bound states in Möbius resonators, reporting that the phase depends on mode. A fourth item reports hybrid graphene plasmon-silica phonon eigenmodes in a graphene ring, forming quadrupolar modes and multiband vortex states. The new element across the set is the framing of accidental BIC existence in terms of parity and nonlocality.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
